# Remarks
The Insert method inserts an item into the ArrayList at a specific location. When we insert an item into an ArrayList, the Count property of the ArrayList is automatically increased by 1.

In our contract test, we're testing if the Insert method works as expected. We are performing an insert into an ArrayList "arrList" at a specific "index". We presume the initial values of the "arrList" and the "index" so we assume an array list "arrList" exists and the "index" is a valid index within the bounds of our array list. After the insert operation, we check the properties of the array list such as Count, the value of the inserted item, the index of the inserted value, and whether the array list contains the inserted value. We use an assertion to state that the values we're monitoring are consistent with our expectations.

In the PexObserve.ValueForViewing, we are storing the initial and the final states of various properties of the array list. This is for debugging and visualization purposes. These are values we get from our assumptions and then verify after the insert operation. We are using these stored values to debug our test.

If the insert operation is correct, we are expecting for the Count of arrList to be increased by 1, and arrList to contain the inserted item. The index in arrList of the inserted item (arrList.IndexOf(x)) must be the same as its last index (arrList.LastIndexOf(x)) which verifies our insert operation works as expected.

To use this test, we would create an instance of ArrayList with known contents and a valid index for the insertion. We then call this method with the known ArrayList and the index where we want x to be inserted. The test will evaluate if the List preserves its state properly after the execution.

This PexSmokeTest method will test our InsertContract, with all sorts of possible inputs. We then visualize that if the insert operation is done correctly on the Array List, the value in the index gets modified to the inserted value, and the Count property is increased by 1.

We also provide assertions ensuring the proper operation of the method as part of the PexSmokeTest method. For instance, the ArrayList does not contain the value x prior to an insertion, but it now does contain the value, and there remains at least one occurrence of the inserted value (since the value was added at the intended index). Also, the IndexOf and LastIndexOf methods should return the same value after the insertion as before the insertion.

To conclude, the PexSmokeTest method performs a unit test of our Insert method, which we expect to work correctly according to our preconditions and postconditions.
# Summary
In this test, we verified the Insert operation working properly in ArrayList after insertion. It checked the index operation after the insertion in ArrayList. It also ensures the ArrayList values after the insertion and provides the valid initial and ending states of various properties for the ArrayList. The test confirms that the Insert operation is correctly inserting the item at the specified index and increasing the Count property of the ArrayList. It also checks if the values in index are matching after an insertion before and after the insertion. # References ## [1] ArrayList - Documentation on ArrayList
# Code
```csharp
using System.Collections;
using NUnit.Framework;
using Pex.Framework;

[TestFixture]
public class ArrayListContractTest
{
    [Test]
    [PexSmokeTest(typeof(ArrayList))]
    public void InsertContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
    {
        AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index <= arrList.Count && index >= 0);

        int Old_arrListCount = arr--------------------            postion_of_x_in_old_arrList = arrList.IndexOf(x);
	    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= postion_of_x_in_old_arrList && postion_of_x_in_old_arrList < Old_arrListCount);

	    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == postion_of_x_in_old_arrList);

            Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListContainsX && New_arrListContainsX);
        }
    }
}
```

これは、`ArrayList` 型の `Insert` メソッドのテストを行うテストクラスです。`TestMethodAttribute` が付いていることに注意してください。この属性を持たないテストメソッドは、単体テストでは実行されません。

このテストによって検証されることは、特定の要素が特定の位置に挿入された場合、ArrayList オブジェクトのカウントが増え、その要素がコンテナ内で見つかる位置が正しく変更されることです。このテストでは、`AssumePrecondition.IsTrue` を使用して、予期される最小値を指定し、`arrList.Count` と `arrList.IndexOf(x)` の最小値を指定しています。

> 注: このテストメソッドは動作を確認しますが、動作を確認した最適解とは限りません。ここで示された制約の中に矛盾があるかを確認してください。

テストは、もともと満たしていた予想値を出力し、同一のアサーションを実行して予想値と実際の値が一致しているかどうかを確認します。ここでのアサーションは、要素 `x` がどこに挿入されたかがわかるかどうかを検査しています。この検査には `Assert.IsTrue` を使用しています。つまり、要素 `x` のインデックスが `arrList.IndexOf(x)` として確認したいわけです。

[^1]: PexObserve は、値を表示する手段を提供し、後で値を表示したときに使用します。この機能は、単体テストをする上で非常に役立ちま�--------------------            PexAssume.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= index && index <= arrList.Count);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that "new_arrList_contains_x" is true
            PexAssert.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that "new_arrList_Count" is "old_arrList_Count + 1"
            PexAssert.AreEqual(New_arrListCount, Old_arrListCount + 1);

	    // a post-condition using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ is the arrList.Count equal 
            PexAssert.AreEqual(arrList.Count, arrList.Count);

	    // a post-condition using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that "new_arrList_Contains_x" is true
            PexAssert.IsTrue(arrList.Contains(x));

	    // a post-condition using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that ...
            PexAssert.IsTrue(arrList.IndexOf(x) == index);

	    // ... (other assertions as appropriate) 
        }
    }
}
```

可以看出，自动化测试中的每个要点都被归类为一个`PexAssume`、`PexAssert`或`PexObserve`断言。通常，这样可以使测试更具有描述性和有帮助。但是，需要明确的是，在某些情况下，`PexAssumeUnderTest`和`PexAssume`在控制测试的执行方面有不同的作用。
PexAssumeUnderTest用于标记方法的测试类的成员（如字段或属性），而PexAssume则用于声明一系列测试条件。PexAssumeUnderTest是设置上下文，而PexAssume是在运行时评估的断言条件，只有在此条件为真的情况下，测试才会继续进行。
总之，在整个测试运行中，我们假设了一些初始的测试条件（PexAssume），然后观察了ArrayList的变化（PexObserve），最后进行了一些断言来验证ArrayList的操作是否按照我们的意图成功（PexAssert）。

**C\# ArrayList Contract Test**

基于上面的测试背景和对Pex的介绍，下面我们将使用Pex来对ArrayList的合同测试，具体的测试方法就是验证ArrayList的Insert方法，测试ArrayList Insert方法的输入参数和输出参数。Pex对这些参数的变化进行观察，然后做出一些断言来验证ArrayList Insert操作的正确性。

```csharp
namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        [TestMethod]
        [PexMethod]
        [PexAnalyzerValidation(Scope = PexScope.AllMembers)]
        [PexExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentException))]
        public void PUT_InsertContract_Test([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, [PexInSource(typeof(ArrayList), "GetRandomInsertArguments", "ArrayInsertArgumentsSource")] GetArrayInputs input)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(input.index <= arrList.Count && input.index >= 0);

            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            arrList.Insert(input.index, input.x);

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;

            // Assert Count is increased
            PexAssert.AreEqual(New_arrListCount, Old_arrListCount + 1);

            // Assert Inserted x equals to input.x 
            PexAssert.IsTrue(arrList[input.index].Equals(input.x));
        }
    }
}

```

在这个测试中，我们首先预设ArrayList的插入索引和插入的值，然后使用Pex进行插入操作，然后使用PexAssert观察ArrayList的元素和Count的变化，最后我们进行一些断言来验证ArrayList Insert操作的正确性。

测试方法的特性PexAttribute可以帮助系统检测到可能的故障和错误。通过使用Pex，我们可以更容易的发现那些我们未知的错误，对我们编写的测试代码有一定增强作用。
Pex的用法介绍就到这里，我们会根据Pex的应用和介绍对此进行更深入的研究和解析；同时--------------------